# A1: Already answered. The reduced value. Always.

This was answered in the previous ANSWERS file. Repeating:

After forcing a scrutinee to WHNF, the mismatch/default branch receives the
forced WHNF value. Always. HVM is LINEAR. The original thunk is consumed and
gone. You cannot reuse it. If you do, you get segfaults and graph corruption
-- which is exactly what was happening in your prior regressions.

Pass the reduced value. This is not ambiguous.
